## Third-party work this project INTEROPERATES WITH

Stated precisely, because the distinction matters legally and we would rather
under-claim: **no third-party source code is vendored into this repository.**
Everything below is a dependency resolved at install time or a separate process
this project talks to over a protocol. Nothing here is redistributed by us.

### TradingAgents — Apache License 2.0
`mizan/adapters/tradingagents.py` is an ADAPTER written from scratch for this
project. It imports nothing from TradingAgents: its only imports are the Python
standard library and `mizan.contracts`. It consumes the SHAPE of a TradingAgents
decision so that framework's output can be governed, which is interoperation,
not derivation. No TradingAgents code is copied, modified or redistributed here,
so the Apache-2.0 redistribution obligations (NOTICE propagation, statement of
modifications) are not triggered. The attribution is recorded anyway because the
interface is theirs and credit is owed for it.

### alpaca-py — Apache License 2.0
Alpaca's official Python SDK, installed as a normal dependency and pinned in
`pyproject.toml`. Used by `mizan/adapters/alpaca_paper.py`. Not vendored.

### alpaca-mcp-server — see the project's own licence
Alpaca's official MCP server. Mizan launches it as a SEPARATE PROCESS and speaks
MCP to it over stdio; it runs in its own environment (`uvx`), which is
deliberate — it keeps that server's dependency versions from moving the pins
recorded in every `DecisionRecord.library_versions`. Not vendored, not modified.

Note, since it is a finding this project reports rather than a criticism made in
passing: that server exposes seven tools which can liquidate an account with no
decision recorded. Mizan makes them unreachable rather than relying on an agent
not to call them. See `docs/MCP-INTERFACE.md`.

### pydantic, jsonschema, PyYAML and other runtime dependencies
Installed dependencies, each under its own licence, pinned in `pyproject.toml`.
The decision-path pins are exact by design (Hard Rule C6) so that a recorded
decision names the exact library versions that produced it.
